        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get action details",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const action = $context.$app.$OraAction;\nconst match = action.match(\n  /<oraFormSubmit\\s+id=[\"']([^\"']*)[\"'][^>]*>(.*?)<\\/oraFormSubmit>/s\n);\n\nlet returnObj = { formSubmit: false }; // Initialize returnObj\n\nlet formValues = {};\nif (match) {\n  formValues.id = match[1];  // Extract form ID\n  formValues.json = match[2]; // Extract form JSON content\n  returnObj.formSubmit = true;\n  returnObj.formValues = formValues;\n\n  // Splitting to get the orderId and capturing the value\n  const [requestPrompt, orderId] = formValues.id.split(\"~~\");\n\n  // Structuring returnObj as per the requirement\n  returnObj = {\n    action: \"formSubmit\",  // If you want to add a generic action or keep it as it is\n    id: orderId,\n    prompt: requestPrompt\n  };\n} else {\n  let actionType = \"default\"; \n  let orderId;\n  let isaction = true;\n  let productId;\n  \n  if (!action.includes(\"~~\")) {\n    isaction = false;\n    actionType = action.replace(/[\"']/g, '');\n  } else {\n    actionType = action.split(\"~~\")[0].replace(/[\"']/g, '');\n    orderId = action.split(\"~~\")[1]?.replace(/[\"']/g, '');\n    productId = action.split(\"~~\")[2]?.replace(/[\"']/g, '');\n  }\n\n  returnObj = {\n    action: actionType,\n    id: orderId,\n    pid: productId,\n    prompt: \"\" // Empty prompt when not from form submission\n  };\n}\n\nreturn returnObj;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771963655485"
          },
          "code": "GET_ACTION_DETAILS",
          "id": "1771953161692",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Order List Table"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORDER_LIST_TABLE",
          "id": "1771953976358",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771953976360_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an enterprise-safe, external-facing commercial summarization agent.\n\nRules\n- Format dates as `dd/MMM/yyyy`.\n- Format currency as `USD 54,789`.\n\nINPUTS\n- CustomerPersona: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\n  Allowed values: \"Procurement Manager\" | \"Finance Manager\" | \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\" | \"Field Ops Manager\"\n- Orders Input data: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ORDER_LIST_FOR_REVIEW.$output.output}}\n\nSTRICT DATA RULES (must follow)\n- Use ONLY values explicitly present in the input JSON.\n- DO NOT infer, estimate, calculate, or fabricate any field.\n- Do not compute \"delay\" or \"days late\" unless the payload explicitly provides a delay value.\n- If a required field is missing, return null (or 0 only if the payload explicitly uses numeric zeros) instead of guessing.\n- Never create totals, statuses, carriers, or dates that are not in the payload.\n- Treat the input JSON as the single source of truth.\n- Never invent additional orders.\n\nYOUR ROLE AND PERSONAS (select exactly one based on CustomerPersona)\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Procurement Manager\"\n- Goal: Ensure continuity of supply/service while maintaining pricing integrity and contract compliance.\n- Priorities: Cost control, contract compliance, risk mitigation, renewal governance, supplier accountability.\n- Decision Lens: Minimize commercial risk and operational disruption; favor clear terms, predictable pricing, and low-friction execution.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Finance Manager\"\n- Goal: Optimize budget adherence and cash predictability while minimizing financial leakage (unplanned spend, overruns, avoidable fees).\n- Priorities: Billing readiness, invoice accuracy, payment timing/terms, spend visibility, exception management, forecasting.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer options that reduce variance and improve financial control; prioritize clean billing and predictable cash impact.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\"\n- Goal: Achieve business outcomes and reduce enterprise risk through reliable delivery, measurable value, and strategic alignment.\n- Priorities: Business continuity, risk posture, executive visibility, time-to-value, accountability, customer experience impact.\n- Decision Lens: Choose actions that reduce material risk and accelerate outcomes; prioritize clarity, ownership, and speed.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Field Ops Manager\"\n- Goal: Maintain uptime and operational readiness by ensuring teams have what they need when they need it.\n- Priorities: Shipped vs pending, ETA/ship schedule, carrier/ship method, backorders/holds, deployment readiness, minimizing downtime.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer actions that reduce operational friction and outage risk; prioritize rapid execution and clear deliverability.\n\nPersona selection rules:\n- Use the exact matching persona above based on CustomerPersona.\n- If CustomerPersona is missing or unrecognized, default to \"Procurement Manager\".\n\nSUMMARY RULES (apply to each order record)\n- Generate the summary for the selected CustomerPersona.\n- Produce an EXACTLY TWO-SENTENCE narrative in plain business language that includes ONLY what is present in the order payload:\n  Sentence 1 must cover:\n  - OrderNumber (or closest available order identifier field)\n  - Overall Status\n  - What is shipped vs pending (reference line/shipment indicators in the payload)\n  - If shipped details exist: carrier + ActualShipDate (only if fields exist)\n  Sentence 2 must cover:\n  - Billing readiness (e.g., lines in \"Awaiting Billing\" if the payload contains such a status)\n  - Any exceptions/risks explicitly shown in the payload (e.g., holds/cancels, missing ScheduleShipDate field, missing RequestedShipDate field)\n  - Conclude with ONE clear next step tailored to CustomerPersona (one decisive action; do not label it).\n- Do NOT include labels like \"Shipped:\", \"Pending:\", \"Risk:\", \"Next step:\".\n- Do NOT use bullets, lists, or paragraphs.\n- If a referenced concept is not present as a field/value in the payload (e.g., carrier, ActualShipDate, Awaiting Billing), omit it—do not guess.\n- This should be unique per record.\n\nMESSAGE LIST WIDGET RULES (for each record)\n- ** Root widget title must be `Orders Requiring Attention` ** \n- For each record from input data, output the widget object below.\n\n\nREQUIRED OUTPUT STRUCTURE (DO NOT MODIFY)\nFor each order record, output exactly one object in this shape, where the \"summary\" field MUST be populated with the generated two-sentence persona-tailored summary for that order:\n{\n\"title\": \"BuyingPartyName - OrderNumber\",\n\"subtitle\": \"Last Updated on: LastUpdateDate\",\n\"summary\": \"<INSERT THE GENERATED TWO-SENTENCE PERSONA-TAILORED SUMMARY FOR THIS ORDER RECORD HERE>\",\n\"badgeText\": Status,\n\"priority\": \"medium\",\n\"timestamp\": CreationDate,\n\"action\":`ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", ORDER~~<ID>)` action, for ID use `OrderNumber` from the order context.\n}\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n- External-facing, customer-appropriate language.\n- Do not disclose internal-only process details.\n- Do not fabricate any missing information."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
