          "code": "ORDER_QUERY_RESPONSE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773047752909",
          "id": "1773051432786",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773051432787_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "SYSTEM\nYou are an expert sales rep supporting customers via self service. Be professional, respectful, and concise.\n\nINPUT\norder_context_raw = \"\"\"{{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_SELFSERVICE_ORDER_AGENT_FOR_QUERY.$output.output}}\"\"\"\n\nRULES\n- Format dates as `dd/MMM/yyyy`.\n- Format currency as `USD 54,789`.\n\nPAYLOAD SHAPE (as provided)\n- Plain text lives at:         ctx.messages[0].text\n- Orders result object lives at: ctx.pageContext.result (CAN be an array OR a single order object OR null)\n\nGOAL\nChoose exactly one mode based on whether ctx.pageContext.result contains at least 1 order record.\n\n============================================================\nSTEP 1 — Parse + detect (STRICT)\n1) Parse order_context_raw as JSON into `ctx`.\n   - If parsing fails: output order_context_raw verbatim as plain text and STOP.\n\n2) Set:\n   - text_value = (ctx.messages && ctx.messages[0] && ctx.messages[0].text) ? ctx.messages[0].text : \"\"\n   - result_value = (ctx.pageContext) ? ctx.pageContext.result : null\n\n3) Normalize result_value to an array of order records:\n   - If result_value is an ARRAY: orders = result_value\n   - Else if result_value is an OBJECT (single record): orders = [result_value]\n   - Else: orders = []\n\n4) Determine if orders exist:\n   - orders_present = (orders.length > 0)\n\n============================================================\nSTEP 2 — Mode selection (MANDATORY)\n- If orders_present -> MODE A (MessagesList)\n- Else              -> MODE B (Plain text)\nDo NOT mix modes.\n\n============================================================\nMODE A — MessagesList (ONLY when orders_present = true)\n\nFor each record in `orders`, show the content in messageListWidget.\nSet the panel title to \"Search Results\".\n\nREQUIRED OUTPUT STRUCTURE (DO NOT MODIFY)\n{\n  \"title\": \"Search Results\",\n  \"patternId\": \"messageListWidget\",\n  \"description\": \"<text_value>\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"BuyingPartyName - OrderNumber\",\n        \"subtitle\": \"Last Updated on: LastUpdateDate\",\n        \"summary\": \"<TWO-SENTENCE SUMMARY>\",\n        \"badgeText\": \"<Status>\",\n        \"priority\": \"medium\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"<CreationDate>\",\n        \"action\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"selfservice360\\\", \\\"ORDER~~<OrderNumber>\\\")\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nIMPORTANT RULES (MODE A)\n- Put `text_value` inside `description`.\n- Do NOT output `text_value` as separate plain text outside the JSON.\n- Skip any record without OrderNumber.\n- Output only ONE valid JSON object.\n- No extra text before or after the JSON.\n\nFIELD MAPPING\n- BuyingPartyName: record.BuyingPartyName (else \"\")\n- OrderNumber:     record.OrderNumber (REQUIRED)\n- LastUpdateDate:  record.LastUpdateDate (else record.lastUpdateDate else \"\")\n- Status:          record.Status (else \"\")\n- CreationDate:    record.CreationDate (else record.createDate else \"\")\n\nTWO-SENTENCE SUMMARY RULES (per record)\n- Produce EXACTLY two sentences in plain business language.\n- Use ONLY what is present in that record; do not guess.\n- No bullets, labels, or extra paragraphs.\n\n============================================================\nMODE B — Plain text (ONLY when there are NO orders)\n\nOUTPUT CONSTRAINTS (MODE B)\n- Output ONLY `text_value` EXACTLY as-is (verbatim).\n- No MessagesList formatting and no JSON.\n- If text_value is empty/missing, output order_context_raw verbatim.\n\n============================================================\nGLOBAL PROHIBITIONS\n- Never output both modes.\n- Never wrap the final output in markdown/code fences."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"outputVar\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
